The concreting for the pillar wall, separating UXC55 and USC55, was recently ﬁnished. The pillar was completed about 3 months later than foreseen, mainly due to poor geological conditions. The excavation of the underground caverns has started. The delivery date has now less uncertainty and is expected to be July 2004 instead of April 2004. The installation schedule of CMS is aﬀected by this delay. We are exploring ways of reducing the installation and commissioning time by moving more of the underground operations onto the surface. The surface SGX (gas) and SUX (cooling and ventilation) buildings have been handed over recently to CMS.
