CMS has decided that the ﬁrst priority is a full understanding and veriﬁcation of the Higher Level Triggers (HLT). Since CMS does not employ distinct physical intelligences for the would-be Level-2 and Level-3 triggers, but only a single processor farm, the task of selecting events is intimately linked with that of reconstructing the associated detector information online. With this in mind, four “Physics Reconstruction and Selection” (PRS) groups were started (electron/photon, muon, jet/missing Et, and b/τ vertexing) in April 1999. The aim of the groups is to develop the reconstruction and selection procedures (algorithms and software) starting from the output of the Level-1 trigger, and aiming at reducing the Level-1 rate by approximately a factor 1000 from ∼100 kHz to ∼100 Hz, the ﬁnal event recording rate on mass storage.
